maybe have to make or find some props. And then go, voila. It has a look of any British synth pop video you might see on MTV in the 1980s. High contrast lighting, graphic wipes, glamorous, melancholy. If you blinked, you might think you were watching a Kajuku music video. And it went down so brilliantly well that they asked us to do more, so we started a little company. In order to keep things within budget, producers needed to get creative. They'd borrow a friend's apartment to shoot in, or work out deals with actors trying to get footage for a demo reel,

